cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the DATE 2022 paper below, which it
  reimplements.
title: "m-rwgan — multi-reward WGAN for heterogeneous network-on-chip design"
abstract: >-
  A reimplementation of M-RWGAN: a Wasserstein GAN steered by several frozen
  reward networks at once — throughput, power and area — generating router-class
  assignments over a fixed mesh, so that design-space exploration returns a
  small set of near-Pareto heterogeneous networks-on-chip rather than one answer.
type: software
